            "message": "Semicolon present; review for clause stacking.",
            "reason": "semicolon",
            "scope": "finance.body",
            "text": "The Chicago Fed NFCI is -0.50 after a 0.02 increase over three months. Borrower strain is 26.0, compared with lender strain of -13.5. Reuters reported that AI credit jitters drove U.S. technology default insurance to record highs, and the Financial Times reported investors selling data-center bonds. These reports identify stress in exposed instruments, but they do not establish system-wide tightening; the strain measures still show a pronounced borrower-lender split."
          },
          {
            "message": "Semicolon present; review for clause stacking.",
            "reason": "semicolon",
            "scope": "grid_storage.body",
            "text": "The active interconnection queue remains 2,061 GW, but only 24.2% is at executed-agreement or construction stages. Storage accounts for 552.7 GW, and only 13% of the 2000\u20132020 queue cohort reached operation. Utility Dive reported that FERC rejected most of PJM\u2019s large-load interconnection plan, days after PJM approved fast-track interconnection for 2.1 GW from Engie and LS Power. Individual projects can advance even while rules for larger-load connections remain unsettled; the decisions do not alter the low historical conversion rate."
          },
          {
            "message": "Semicolon present; review for clause stacking.",
            "reason": "semicolon",
            "scope": "water.body",
            "text": "Of campuses with county drought data, 280, or 19.5%, are in counties where at least 25% of the area is under D2-or-worse drought; both the count and share decreased materially. The broader screen\u2014any D2-or-worse area in the county\u2014covers 345 campuses, or 24.1%, and decreased slightly. These measures track county geography, not campus water consumption or the exact location of drought within a county."
          },
          {
            "message": "Semicolon present; review for clause stacking.",
            "reason": "semicolon",
            "scope": "macro.paragraphs[2]",
            "text": "Downstream diffusion remains less decisive. Businesses expecting AI use within six months edged up to 27.7%, but this is 3.9 percentage points above current use. Only one tracked AI-linked labor channel has positive employment growth, with power and communication construction leading at 0.8%. Nonfarm-business productivity is growing 2.2%, while real hourly compensation is growing 0.6%; these aggregate measures do not identify AI\u2019s contribution. The data therefore show positive productivity and a modest rise in adoption expectations, but not broad labor-market diffusion or a demonstrated economy-wide AI effect."
          }
        ],
